[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133961508","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4133961508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4133961508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72Zz8k","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T11:46:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T11:59:30Z","body":"I just tried the pure math function benchmark found in #117121, and I'm seeing very similar numbers to that PR, with both showing a ~20% speedup on my machine","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133961508/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4134861558","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4134861558","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4134861558,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72dPr2","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T13:35:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T21:53:22Z","body":"> I'll see if I can provide some hard numbers from Tracy later on\r\n\r\nThis is from running the above mentioned benchmark in a real-world project based on 4.6.1-stable, which just runs through a replay of the game over and over, so should hopefully be somewhat representative of real-world use. Although, this particular project makes heavy use of custom `Resource` classes and `RefCounted` in general.\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"620\" height=\"40\" alt=\"Before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/236e146a-07d5-4d94-be77-1c82ad283819\" />\r\n\r\nAfter:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"619\" height=\"42\" alt=\"After\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cebc2ec6-62b0-49e4-ad35-3066a1faac90\" />\r\n\r\nThe time/percentages shown is the total time spent in those particular functions throughout the entire benchmark, so the improvement is closer to 5%.\r\n\r\nI have another change lined up that should yield another couple of percentage points though, as there's a bunch more needless `RefCounted` copies happening in `GDScriptFunction::call`, from things like `get_script().ptr()` and `get_base_script().ptr()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4134861558/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136253492","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4136253492","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4136253492,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72ijg0","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T16:06:24Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T16:06:24Z","body":"> but we should probably add some comments\r\n\r\nDone. Let me know if I should add some more.\r\n\r\n> My biggest concern was `NIL`\r\n\r\nI hope I haven't misunderstood the purpose of the `NIL` entry, but isn't it always supposed to be an empty `Variant` by definition?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136253492/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136308868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4136308868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4136308868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72ixCE","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T16:14:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T16:14:09Z","body":"So I'd say for `CLASS` this is safe, since `GDScript` does generally not get destructed anyway. Also `GDScriptInstance` holds a reference to its script.\r\n\r\nFor `SELF` I'm not entirely sure. There is no direct reference, so we would be relying on the caller to ensure that the object does not get freed during a call. This _should_ be fine I think.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136308868/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136430169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4136430169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4136430169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72jOpZ","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T16:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T16:31:18Z","body":"> I hope I haven't misunderstood the purpose of the `NIL` entry, but isn't it always supposed to be an empty `Variant` by definition?\r\n\r\nSee #117863 for details. We already have a separate address mode for constants, I don't think the specific constant `null` requires a fixed address for optimization or something like that.\r\n\r\nI think the fixed address `NIL` exists only because there's a corresponding `NIL` address mode (we could rename it to `NONE`). This mode is used, for example, for calling `void` functions or when the return value isn't needed (but we still need a temporary `Variant` for the function result). The funny thing is that we can't use the fixed `NIL` address for the `NIL` address mode (as a destination address) because that address still needs to be cleared and is also occasionally used as a constant (as a source address). So, a temporary is used instead of the fixed `NIL` address.\r\n\r\nThis isn't directly related to your PR, but I answered as you asked.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136430169/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136806530","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4136806530","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4136806530,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72kqiC","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T17:24:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T19:14:38Z","body":"> For `SELF` I'm not entirely sure. There is no direct reference, so we would be relying on the caller to ensure that the object does not get freed during a call. This _should_ be fine I think.\r\n\r\nI went ahead and tried to force this to become a problem, and I am indeed able to force an AddressSanitizer (`use_asan=yes`) crash with the following code, at `self.some_state += 1`, which previously worked fine:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nclass_name SomeParent extends Node\r\n\r\nclass SomeChild extends RefCounted:\r\n\tvar parent: SomeParent\r\n\tvar some_state := 0\r\n\r\n\tfunc cause_crash():\r\n\t\tself.parent.child = null\r\n\t\tself.some_state += 1\r\n\r\nvar child: SomeChild\r\n\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tself.child = SomeChild.new()\r\n\tself.child.parent = self\r\n\tself.child.cause_crash()\r\n```\r\n\r\nHow much of a problem do we consider this kind of scenario to be?\r\n\r\nWe could maybe have a local `Ref` in `GDScriptFunction::call`, only in `DEBUG_ENABLED`, and check its reference count at the end, and emit some error message if this is the sole remaining reference? It might not be foolproof in multi-threaded scenarios though, and it could be considered a breaking change.\r\n\r\n> This mode is used, for example, for calling `void` functions or when the return value isn't needed (but we still need a temporary `Variant` for the function result).\r\n\r\nIt sounds like it's a bit more involved than I thought. Just let me know if I should have the destructor loop start at `ADDR_STACK_NIL` instead of `FIXED_ADDRESSES_MAX`. It changes nothing about this PR, apart from keeping the potentially redundant call to a no-op destructor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136806530/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4137171295","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4137171295","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4137171295,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72mDlf","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T18:13:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T18:13:12Z","body":"> We could maybe have a local `Ref` in `GDScriptFunction::call`, only in `DEBUG_ENABLED`, and check its reference count at the end, and emit some error message if this is the sole remaining reference?\r\n\r\nI should note that we already sort of do this with non-`RefCounted` objects, where we have `OBJ_DEBUG_LOCK` in `DEBUG_ENABLED` builds to stop you from trying to free objects whose methods are currently being called, among other things:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a1aa0fa2fa13a3c28de232a08bb8074086abf1f4/core/object/object.cpp#L770-L774","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4137171295/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4137248403","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4137248403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4137248403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72mWaT","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T18:23:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T18:23:38Z","body":"The correct way to avoid a crash like this is to reference the `self` on call, as if it was a parameter.\nNormally this should happen at the caller site. Which I assumed was already happening.\nSince it's, i think can merge this. The callee being referenced (in general) is a requirement for same ownership logic.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4137248403/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4137276180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4137276180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4137276180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72mdMU","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T18:27:58Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T18:28:34Z","body":"A way to salvage this might actually be to insert the reference at the caller site.\nLike I said, it's illegal to call a function without guaranteeing the lifetime of all objects within to at least the end of the function. Since the caller is currently not doing this, they're violating that contract.\nIf the caller was made to adhere to the contract, we could merge this optimization. The GDScript VM would be able to avoid a superfluous refcount increase on call if the caller is guaranteed to outlive the function - which i think should be most cases, except those where a field is used as callee (as seen in your artificial crash).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4137276180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138014521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4138014521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4138014521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72pRc5","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T20:30:19Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T20:31:03Z","body":"> A way to salvage this might actually be to insert the reference at the caller site.\r\n\r\nThe `SomeParent` class in my example could presumably just as well be from a GDExtension, and I assume the crash would happen in that scenario too. However we feel about what the contract *should* be in this case, the current behavior might be well-established enough that this is too breaking of a change.\r\n\r\nBut again, we should be able to fairly easily detect that this kind of thing is happening (in `DEBUG_ENABLED`), assuming everyone agrees that this is just a bug and that it should be loudly reported to the user as such. If not, then I'm fine with scaling this back to only cover `ADDR_STACK_CLASS` for now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138014521/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138143396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4138143396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4138143396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72pw6k","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T20:54:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T20:54:16Z","body":"> The `SomeParent` class in my example could presumably just as well be from a GDExtension, and I assume the crash would happen in that scenario too. However we feel about what the contract _should_ be in this case, the current behavior might be well-established enough that this is too breaking of a change.\r\n\r\nTrue. Though this quickly goes into language design territory - is GDScript protected against memory errors or no? So far, it _mostly_ is (but not entirely).\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138143396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138232823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4138232823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4138232823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72qGv3","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T21:10:44Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T21:10:44Z","body":"> If not, then I'm fine with scaling this back to only cover `ADDR_STACK_CLASS` for now.\r\n\r\nI'd say let's split this in two PRs. It would be a shame if we end up reverting this because of `SELF` and also loose the safe `CLASS` improvement.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138232823/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138520175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4138520175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4138520175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72rM5v","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T21:52:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T21:52:29Z","body":"> I'd say let's split this in two PRs. It would be a shame if we end up reverting this because of `SELF` and also loose the safe `CLASS` improvement.\r\n\r\nI've scaled this PR back to only cover `ADDR_STACK_CLASS` now, i.e. the safe subset. I left `ADDR_STACK_NIL` alone this time around as well, since it seemed to be bound for removal anyway (#117863).\r\n\r\nHere's the new (less impressive) before and after in our real-world benchmark:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"631\" height=\"35\" alt=\"Before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/03d74c3b-0385-4002-a924-88eb3630e72c\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"633\" height=\"40\" alt=\"After\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c69c72f-3f23-4775-b502-9c01ab54b959\" />\r\n\r\n(Again, this particular project makes heavy use of custom `Resource` classes and `RefCounted` in general.)\r\n\r\nI'll make a new PR for `ADDR_STACK_SELF` once this is merged, and we can continue that discussion there.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138520175/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4157370242","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4157370242","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4157370242,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73zG-C","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-30T18:52:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-30T18:52:06Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4157370242/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4172789864","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4172789864","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117850","id":4172789864,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74t7ho","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T20:30:22Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T20:30:22Z","body":"Just in case there was any interest in this, I've put up a new PR for the `ADDR_STACK_SELF` part that I removed from this PR, along with the `DEBUG_ENABLED`-only error-checking that I [mentioned](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#issuecomment-4136806530) above: #118086","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4172789864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]